<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-qinzong"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Qinzong</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Qinzong was the ninth emperor of the Song dynasty of China, reigning from 1126 to 1127 after his father Huizong abdicated during the Jurchen invasion.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-ruizong-of-tang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-ruizong-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Ruizong of Tang</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Ruizong of Tang (662–716), born Li Dan, was a son of Emperor Gaozong and Wu Zetian.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shengzong-of-liao"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Shengzong of Liao</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Shengzong of Liao, Yelü Longxu, was the sixth emperor of the Khitan Liao dynasty, reigning from 982 to 1031.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-shenzong-of-song"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-shenzong-of-song.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Shenzong of Song</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Shenzong was an emperor of the Northern Song in the late eleventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-shirakawa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-shirakawa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Shirakawa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Shirakawa was the 72nd emperor of Japan according to the traditional order of succession, reigning from 1073 to 1087.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/ency