iao"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Taizu of Liao</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yelü Abaoji, Emperor Taizu of Liao, was the Khitan leader who founded the Liao dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-taizu-of-song.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Taizu of Song</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Taizu, born Zhao Kuangyin, was the founder of the Song Dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-tenmu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-tenmu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Tenmu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Tenmu (c. 631–686) was the 40th emperor of Japan, reigning from 673 to 686.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-tianzuo-of-liao"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Tianzuo of Liao</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Tianzuo (Yelü Yanxi) was the ninth and last emperor of the Liao dynasty, reigning from 1101 to 1125.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-uda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-uda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Uda</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Emperor Uda was the 59th emperor of Japan according to the traditional order of succession, reigning from 887 to 897.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-han"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-wen-of-han.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Emperor Wen of Han</span><span class="enc-type">Perso